---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/12-01/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/12-01/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/12-01/',photo='https://www.zeiss.com/microscopy/en/products/light-microscopes/stereo-and-zoom-microscopes/stereo-discovery-v12.html',optics='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/2a32330d-32e6-40a6-9690-c32339717e15/EN_IM_SteREO_Discovery_V05_IVD.pdf',catalog='https://www.micro-shop.zeiss.com/en/us/system/stereo%2Bdiscovery-stereo%2Bdiscovery.v12-stereomicroscopes/10155/';
const display=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(9)):v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS Discovery.V12 stereo ruler" subtitle="" description="Inspect the ZEISS Discovery.V12 form and see an inert height marker from two ideal stereo views." wide={true}>
<article id="v12" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-01/">← Equipment 12-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#v12-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">12-01 / ZEISS SteREO Discovery.V12 / Manufactured ruler</p><h2>ZEISS Discovery.V12</h2><p>Inspect an inert 1 mm grid and a 2 mm raised marker through paired geometric views. Doubling zoom doubles the pixel spacing of the grid and scale bar, and the raised marker shifts left-to-right between the two views.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the microscope</h3><div id="v12-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Ruler','Oculars'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="v12-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="v12-model" aria-label="Orbitable metric Discovery.V12 with binocular head, zoom panel and grid plate"></canvas><p id="v12-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the small panel on the right to cycle virtual zoom, an ocular to read the pair, or the plate to mark ruler origin. Drag to orbit and scroll or pinch to zoom.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Compare nominal zoom</h3><div class="e-fields"><label>Zoom body<select id="v12-zoom">{[.8,1.6,3.2,6.4,10].map(k=><option value={k}>{k}×</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="e-row"><button id="v12-cycle" class="e-run" type="button">Next zoom</button><button id="v12-center" type="button">Mark ruler center</button><button id="v12-reset" type="button">Reset</button></div>
<p id="v12-status" role="status">Ready to inspect the manufactured grid.</p><p id="v12-result" role="status">No fit data.</p><p id="v12-pointer" role="status">Click either view or choose ruler center to read coordinates.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="v12-json" disabled>Export stereo geometry JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Compare the binocular pair</h3><div class="e-grid stereo"><figure><svg id="v12-L" viewBox="0 0 480 320" role="img" aria-label="Geometric left view of the ruler and elevated gold fiducial"></svg><figcaption>Left view</figcaption></figure><figure><svg id="v12-R" viewBox="0 0 480 320" role="img" aria-label="Geometric right view of the ruler and elevated gold fiducial"></svg><figcaption>Right view</figcaption></figure></div><p>Each green grid interval is 1 mm. Gold represents the raised marker. At high zoom the marked point may leave the field; the table still reports its extrapolated position. Click to get a point on the flat ruler plane, not to measure height. <a href={a+'example-view.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Selected configuration and references</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Discovery.V12 front geometry"/><figcaption>Original reconstruction based on <a href={photo}>ZEISS’s Discovery.V12 assembly photograph</a>. The photographed objective may differ from the documented example below; exterior and stand envelope are inferred.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original objective, illumination base and manufactured scale"/><figcaption>Original metric objective and ruler placement. Visible front rim approximates the nominal working gap.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Zoom body</td><td>0.8–10×, 76 mm mount</td><td><a href={catalog}>ZEISS V12 body 435001-9901-000</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>Example objective and eyepiece</td><td>PlanApo S 1×, PL 10×/23, 60 mm nominal working distance</td><td><a href={optics}>ZEISS Technical Data, Optical data of SteREO Discovery.V12</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>Nominal horizontal field</td><td>29 mm at 0.8×; about 2.3 mm at 10×</td><td>Same objective/eyepiece row. The virtual chart scales 23.2/zoom mm.</td></tr><tr><td>Stereo geometry</td><td>±6° illustrative projection, not a measured angle</td><td>Original orthographic calibration demonstration.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>Model and limits</h3><p>The grid plane has zero model disparity. In each ideal view the horizontal coordinate is proportional to X ± Z tan 6°; positive height shifts the left view rightward relative to the right view. This tests calibration and disparity direction, not resolution, distortion, depth of field, optical transfer, or empirical depth accuracy. This pass uses only a manufactured ruler and no biological material.</p></section>
<section id="v12-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'zeiss-discovery-v12.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-01/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#v12 header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#v12 h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#v12 section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#v12 button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#v12 button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#v12-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#v12-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#v12 table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#v12 td,#v12 th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#v12 figure{margin:0}#v12 img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#v12 caption{text-align:left}#v12 input,#v12 select,#v12 button{min-width:0}#v12 .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#v12 .stereo svg{width:100%;height:auto;background:#e7e7dc;display:block;overflow:hidden;cursor:crosshair}#v12 .stereo figcaption{margin:.3rem 0}</style>
